  m_Text: "I know this was no isolated spectacle. This scene was replayed too many
    times, all over Europe. Approximately 50,000 \u2013 mostly women \u2013 were
    burned at the stake in the late 16th-early 17th centuries. Often, the 'witches'
    confessed - a confession extracted by torture. The history of witchcraft is the
    history of arbitrary law and power. The archives tell the story from above. I
    seek and will hear the screams in the flames.\r"
